CUBE.HTML LICENSE — ALL RIGHTS RESERVED

This is not an open source license. Nothing here is libre.

Copyright law still stands in this — all of it, everywhere, including
the parts you were hoping didn't apply to a funny cube simulator.

1. NO FORKING

   You may not fork this repository. The fork button is not yours.
   You may not fork it "just to look". You may not fork it "to archive
   it" or "for preservation". You may not fork it at all.

2. NO DOWNLOADING

   You may not download, clone, scrape, mirror, save-as, curl, wget, or
   otherwise obtain a copy of this source code. Neither it's audio files. Opening devtools and
   reading the void is tolerated — you were going to do it anyway — but
   you may not take it with you.

3. WHAT IS GRANTED

   One (1) non-transferable right: to view the rendered page at its
   official GitHub Pages URL, for as long as GitHub Pages remains free.

4. WHY THIS LICENSE EXISTS

   This repository is hosted on GitHub for exactly one reason: GitHub
   Pages exists and is free. Static site hosting costs roughly $360 a
   year, and nobody is paying $360 a year to keep a funny cube
   simulator up. If GitHub Pages ever stops being free, this repo gets
   deleted, and that is just the way it goes.

5. THE PASSPHRASE

   You will not find the admin passphrase in this source code. What you
   will find is a sha-256 digest, staring at you, judging you. Do not
   dictionary-attack the void. It has had a long day.

6. THE ARCHIVE EXCEPTION

   Notwithstanding clause 1, the repository known as "retroobj" is
   expressly legal. It is an archive of the first commit of this
   repository — a fossil, frozen in time — and it does not count as a
   fork or a download. One (1) archive is allowed. It is the original
   sin and it stays.

7. THE REST

   All other rights are reserved by lux (and/or obj, who picked his own
   name and needs no permission from you).

   Clicking the cube is legal. Enjoying the cube is legal.
   "obj: ow." is legal.

   Forking is not.
